course: dictionary
lesson: 12613
title: Spotting a discrepancy
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A discrepancy is a difference between two things that should be the same, such as two numbers, accounts or stories. «There is a discrepancy between the two totals: one says 45 and the other says 54.» The totals should match, but they do not.
explain: A discrepancy also shows that something may be wrong. «Sam said he got home at six, but his mum said he came in at eight.» That discrepancy makes the detective ask questions, because one of the stories may be false.
explain: When you find a discrepancy, ask two things: what is different, and why? To explain the discrepancy, you look for the reason the two things do not match, such as a counting mistake, a wrong measurement or a lie.
fact: A discrepancy is a difference between things that should match.
fact: Discrepancy is a noun. The plural is discrepancies.
fact: In science, a discrepancy is a difference between the expected result and the measured result.
fact: In money, a discrepancy is a difference between the amount in the till and the amount on the receipts.
fact: Useful phrases: «a discrepancy between» and «explain the discrepancy».
exercise: «There is a discrepancy between the two totals.» What is a discrepancy? | A sum you get by adding two numbers | A very large answer | *A difference between two things that should be the same
exercise: Mia counts 30 sweets in the jar, but the list says 25. What is the discrepancy? | Mia likes sweets | The jar is red | *The difference of 5 between the count and the list
exercise: «The detective asked why there was a discrepancy in the two stories.» Find and copy the word that means the stories do not match. | stories | *discrepancy | detective | asked
test: «The till said £20, but the receipts added up to £15.» What is the discrepancy? | *A difference of £5 between the till and the receipts | The shop is closed | A difference of £35 | The receipts are white
test: Sofia expected 15 cm but measured 12 cm. What is the discrepancy she should explain? | 27 cm | *3 cm, the difference between expected and measured | 12 cm | It was fine, so nothing to explain
exam: «The two witnesses gave different times, which showed a discrepancy.» What does the discrepancy show? | They agreed completely | The witnesses are friends | Time was very long | *Something may be wrong
